<h1>Register</h1>
<% if (typeof error !== 'undefined' && error) { %><p class="error-box"><%= error %></p><% } %>
<form method="post" action="/register" class="form narrow">
  <label>Username <input name="username" required></label>
  <label>Password <input name="password" type="password" required></label>
  <label>Email <input name="email" type="email"></label>
  <!-- VULN (A06, mass assignment): role reaches the INSERT. -->
  <label>Role <input name="role" value="customer"></label>
  <button type="submit">Create account</button>
</form>
<p class="muted">The “Role” field is here so the mass-assignment lab is obvious. A real form would not have it — the attack then uses an extra form field or a crafted POST.</p>